digits(int)|fDesc:For integer types: number of non-sign bits (radix base digits) in the representation.For floating types: number of digits (in radix base) in the mantissa (equivalent to FLT_MANT_DIG, DBL_MANT_DIG or LDBL_MANT_DIG).[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
digits10(int)|fDesc:Number of digits (in decimal base) hat can be represented without change. Equivalent to FLT_DIG, DBL_DIG or LDBL_DIG for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_digits10(int)|fDesc:Number of digits (in decimal base) required to ensure that values that differ are always differentiated.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_signed(bool)|fDesc:true if type is signed.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_integer(bool)|fDesc:true if type is integer.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_exact(bool)|fDesc:true if type uses exact representations.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
radix(int)|fDesc:For integer types: base of the representation. For floating types: base of the exponent of the representation (equivalent to FLT_RADIX).[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
epsilon()|fDesc:Machine epsilon (the difference between 1 and the least value greater than 1 that is representable). Equivalent to FLT_EPSILON, DBL_EPSILON or LDBL_EPSILON for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_error()|fDesc: Measure of the maximum rounding error.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
min_exponent(int)|fDesc:Minimum negative integer value such that radix raised to (min_exponent-1) generates a normalized floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MIN_EXP, DBL_MIN_EXP or LDBL_MIN_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
min_exponent10(int)|fDesc:Minimum negative integer value such that 10 raised to that power generates a normalized floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MIN_10_EXP, DBL_MIN_10_EXP or LDBL_MIN_10_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_exponent(int)|fDesc:Maximum integer value such that radix raised to (max_exponent-1) generates a representable finite floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MAX_EXP, DBL_MAX_EXP or LDBL_MAX_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
max_exponent10(int)|fDesc:Maximum integer value such that 10 raised to that power generates a normalized finite floating-point number.Equivalent to FLT_MAX_10_EXP, DBL_MAX_10_EXP or LDBL_MAX_10_EXP for floating types.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_infinity(bool)|fDesc:true if the type has a representation for positive infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_quiet_NaN(bool)|fDesc:true if the type has a representation for a quiet (non-signaling) Not-a-Number.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_signaling_NaN(bool)|fDesc:true if the type has a representation for a signaling Not-a-Number.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_denorm(float_denorm_style)|fDesc:Denormalized values -representations with a variable number of exponent bits-. A type may have any of the following enum values:
denorm_absent|fDesc: if it does not allow denormalized values.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_present|fDesc: if it allows denormalized values.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_indeterminate|fDesc: if indeterminate at compile time.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
has_denorm_loss(bool)|fDesc:true if a loss of accuracy is detected as a denormalization loss, rather than an inexact result.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
infinity()|fDesc: Representation of positive infinity, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
quiet_NaN()|fDesc: Representation of quiet (non-signaling) Not-a-Number, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
signaling_NaN()|fDesc: Representation of signaling Not-a-Number, if available.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
denorm_min()|fDesc: Minimum positive denormalized value.For types not allowing denormalized values: same as min().[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_iec559(bool)|fDesc:true if the type adheres to IEC-559 / IEEE-754 standard.An IEC-559 type always has has_infinity, has_quiet_NaN and has_signaling_NaN set to true; And infinity, quiet_NaN and signaling_NaN return some non-zero value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_bounded(bool)|fDesc:true if the set of values represented by the type is finite.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
is_modulo(bool)|fDesc:true if the type is modulo. A type is modulo if it is possible to add two positive numbers and have a result that wraps around to a third number that is less.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
traps(bool)|fDesc:true if trapping is implemented for the type.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
tinyness_before(bool)|fDesc:true if tinyness is detected before rounding.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_style|fDesc:Rounding style. see round_.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
float_round_style|fDesc:	Rounding style. see round_.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_zero|fDesc: if it rounds toward zero.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_to_nearest|fDesc: if it rounds to the nearest representable value.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_infinity|fDesc: if it rounds toward infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_toward_neg_infinity|fDesc: if it rounds toward negative infinity.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|
round_indeterminate|fDesc: if the rounding style is indeterminable at compile time.[c99 cpp98 cpp11]|

